# DigiSwasthya Product Definition Document (PDD)

# Part 14 — Dashboards & KPIs

---

# Purpose

This section defines every dashboard, card, graph, and KPI in DigiSwasthya.

For each:

- Who sees it
- What it shows
- Calculation source
- Default period
- Drill-down destination
- Refresh expectation (product-level)

Dashboards never become the source of truth. Underlying entities do.

---

# Dashboard Principles

1. One primary job per dashboard.
2. KPI definitions must match Business Calculations.
3. Role-appropriate only.
4. Cards drill to filtered lists.
5. No counterparty private data leakage.
6. Empty states are explicit.

---

# 1. Pharmacy Home Dashboard

## Audience

Pharmacy Owner, Manager; Staff/Accountant see permitted cards.

## Purpose

Give an operational snapshot of purchasing, deliveries, payables, and alerts.

## Cards

| Card | Definition | Drill-down |
|---|---|---|
| Pending Orders | Count orders in Pending/Accepted/Packed/Dispatched/Partially Delivered | Orders filtered |
| Awaiting Delivery | Dispatched + Partially Delivered count | Deliveries/Orders |
| Outstanding Payables | Pharmacy Outstanding amount | Invoices outstanding > 0 |
| Overdue Payables | Overdue Amount | Overdue invoices |
| Open Returns | Returns not Closed/Rejected terminal | Returns list |
| Available Credit | Sum remaining credit notes | Credit notes remaining > 0 |
| Unread Notifications | Unread count | Notifications |
| Low Stock (Pharmacy inventory) | Count low-stock products | Inventory low stock |
| Near Expiry | Count/value near-expiry batches | Inventory expiry |

## Graphs

| Graph | Definition |
|---|---|
| Spend Trend | Spend by day/week/month for selected period |
| Orders Placed Trend | Orders submitted over period |
| Payables Aging | Outstanding buckets: 0–30, 31–60, 61–90, 90+ |
| Top Suppliers by Spend | Rank stockists by spend |

## Default Period

Last 30 days for trends; point-in-time for outstanding/open counts.

